		{"id":"model-timeline-frame","type":"group","x":-3960,"y":-220,"width":1860,"height":4023,"label":"Model"},
		{"id":"rope-positions","type":"file","file":"Growth Space/Projects/Software/ML/wan-dit-lab/docs/research/mvp1/RoPE-positions.md","x":3900,"y":-180,"width":1700,"height":2482},
		{"id":"compilation","type":"text","text":"<span class=\"wan-scene-style wan-scene-math wan-scene-grid\"></span>\n# Compilation · MVP1\n\nConsider the computation graph of one DiT block.\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{G=(V,E)}_{\\text{computation graph}},\\qquad\n\\underbrace{V}_{\\text{operations}},\\quad\n\\underbrace{E}_{\\text{data dependencies}}.\n$$\n\n| Transformation | Context → computation | Idea | Observations |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| $\\displaystyle \\mathrm{SDPA}\\mapsto\\mathrm{Sage\\,2}$ | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&\\text{Consider the self- and cross-attention of the block.}\\[6pt]&\\mathrm{Attn}_{\\rm self}=\\mathrm{Attn}_{\\rm cross}=\\mathrm{Sage\\,2}\\[5pt]&\\mathrm{Linear}=\\mathrm{Nunchaku\\ W4A4}\\end{aligned}$ | We choose the kernels of the graph operations. | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&\\underbrace{T_{\\rm block}:186.8\\to77.3\\ \\mathrm{ms}}_{\\text{only self-attention replaced}}\\[6pt]&\\underbrace{704\\times1280,\\quad\\mathrm{FP8}}_{\\text{comparison conditions E29}}\\end{aligned}$<br>[E29](notes/research/cards/E29.%20%D0%92%D0%B5%D1%80%D1%88%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B0%20A%E2%80%B2%20%D0%B8%20%D1%81%D0%BF%D1%83%D1%81%D0%BA%20B,%20FP8,%20704%C3%971280.md) |\n| $\\displaystyle (W_Q,W_K,W_V)\\mapsto W_{\\rm QKV}$ | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&\\text{Consider the three self-attention projections of the input }X.\\[6pt]&W_{\\rm QKV}^{\\top}=[W_Q^{\\top}\\ W_K^{\\top}\\ W_V^{\\top}]\\[5pt]&b_{\\rm QKV}=[b_Q\\ b_K\\ b_V]\\[5pt]&(Q,K,V)=\\mathrm{split}(XW_{\\rm QKV}^{\\top}+b_{\\rm QKV})\\end{aligned}$ | One main GEMM instead of three; the input is quantized once. | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&T_{\\rm QKV}:4.32\\to3.77\\ \\mathrm{ms}\\[5pt]&\\underbrace{\\text{block 0, 7040 tokens}}_{\\text{separate measurement E24}}\\end{aligned}$<br>[E24](notes/research/cards/E24.%20%D0%A1%D0%BB%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%8B%D0%B5%20QKV%20%D0%B8%20FFN%20%D0%B2%20W4A4,%20RoPE%20%D0%B2%D0%BE%20float32,%20704%C3%971280.md) · [Implementation](src/wan_dit_lab/quantization/w4a4.py) |\n| $\\displaystyle \\mathrm{FFN}\\mapsto\\mathrm{FFN}_{\\rm fused}$ | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&\\text{Consider the two linear layers of the FFN.}\\[6pt]&\\underbrace{\\mathrm{GEMM}_1\\to\\mathrm{GELU}\\to\\mathrm{Quant}_4}_{\\text{first GEMM with a fused epilogue}}\\[4pt]&\\qquad\\to\\mathrm{GEMM}_2\\end{aligned}$ | In the epilogue we also compute the projection of the low-rank branch of the second layer; the intermediate hidden is not written in 16 bits. | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&T_{\\rm FFN}:12.70\\to10.67\\ \\mathrm{ms}\\[5pt]&\\underbrace{\\text{block 0, 7040 tokens}}_{\\text{separate measurement E24}}\\end{aligned}$<br>[E24](notes/research/cards/E24.%20%D0%A1%D0%BB%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%8B%D0%B5%20QKV%20%D0%B8%20FFN%20%D0%B2%20W4A4,%20RoPE%20%D0%B2%D0%BE%20float32,%20704%C3%971280.md) · [Implementation](ops/w4a4_ops.cpp) |\n| $\\displaystyle \\mathrm{RoPE}\\overset{\\rm fuse}{\\hookrightarrow}\\mathrm{Attn}_{\\rm Sage}$ | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&\\text{Consider the preparation of }Q,K\\text{ for Sage.}\\[6pt]&\\mathrm{RMSNorm}\\to\\mathrm{RoPE}\\to\\mathrm{Quant}_{\\rm INT8}^{Q,K}\\[4pt]&\\qquad\\to\\mathrm{Attn}_{\\rm Sage}\\end{aligned}$ | We rotate Q/K while preparing the quantized data for Sage. | The RMS statistics are computed in a separate pass.<br>[Implementation](src/wan_dit_lab/kernels/sage_rope.py) |\n| $\\displaystyle G\\xrightarrow{\\mathcal O}G'\\xrightarrow{\\mathcal C_{\\rm compile}}\\mathrm{package}$ | $\\displaystyle \\begin{aligned}&\\text{Consider the graph after the choice of kernels and fusions.}\\[6pt]&G'\\xrightarrow{\\rm torch.export}G_{\\rm FX}\\[5pt]&G_{\\rm FX}\\xrightarrow{\\rm AOTInductor}\\mathrm{package}\\end{aligned}$ | We build a package for running; QKV, FFN and RoPE are enabled independently. | [Live 1](configs/live.json) · [Export](scripts/conversion/export_live.py) |\n","x":5740,"y":-180,"width":1700,"height":1152},
